🌍  AI MARKET RESEARCH REPORT GENERATOR
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
⚡ One product. One country. One click. One report.


🎯 THE PROBLEM
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Launching a product in a new country is risky.
Businesses need to know demand, competitors, pricing and entry
risks, but manual research takes days and agencies charge
thousands.

💡 THE SOLUTION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
A clean web tool where the user:

  1️⃣  Enters a Product Name, Region and Country
  2️⃣  Presses "Generate Report"
  3️⃣  Reads an AI-written research report right on the page
  4️⃣  Downloads it as report.md to share, edit or archive


👥 WHO NEEDS THIS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
📦 Exporters and importers checking a new country
🛒 E-commerce and Amazon sellers comparing markets
🚀 Startups without a research budget
📊 Consultants and agencies who want faster first drafts


💼 WHY IT MATTERS TO A BUSINESS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
✔ Faster first-pass market research, in minutes instead of days
✔ Helps teams decide which markets deserve a deeper look
✔ A repeatable tool anyone on the team can use
✔ A downloadable report that is easy to share with partners


🛠️ WHAT I BUILT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
🐍 Backend: Python + FastAPI
🎨 Frontend: hand-written HTML + CSS, modern and mobile-friendly
🚫 No JavaScript: server-rendered, so it is simple, fast and
   easy to maintain
🔒 Safe output: raw HTML inside AI reports is blocked, so the
   output can't inject markup
🔌 Plug-in AI: one clearly marked function connects the AI
   assistant, so the engine can be upgraded or swapped later


🧠 SKILLS DEMONSTRATED
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Python  •  FastAPI  •  Jinja2  •  HTML5  •  CSS3
Responsive Design  •  AI / LLM Integration
Form Handling and Validation  •  File Download Endpoints
Clean Project Structure  •  UI / UX Design


🏔️ PROJECT DIFFICULTY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Backend API design + AI integration + secure rendering + a
custom-designed UI, all without a JavaScript framework. Keeping
the stack this lean was a deliberate choice for reliability and
low maintenance.


